WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.461
<v Examiner>Pharmacology.

2
00:00:02.461 --> 00:00:03.189
<v Examiner>Module 9.

3
00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:06.423
<v Examiner>Licit and illicit drugs, and toxicology.

4
00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:07.132
Hey.

5
00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:12.445
This is the Module 9 episode of the SAQ podcast, for Introduction to Pharmacology.

6
00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:17.628
Module 9 was the self-directed session on Wednesday the twenty-first of October,

7
00:00:17.628 --> 00:00:20.414
the afternoon the lecturers were on strike.

8
00:00:20.414 --> 00:00:21.645
Nobody lectured it.

9
00:00:21.645 --> 00:00:27.023
Joan put one slide deck on Canvas, forty-one slides, and this episode is that deck,

10
00:00:27.023 --> 00:00:29.615
turned into the answers you would write.

11
00:00:30.065 --> 00:00:30.959
Why it matters.

12
00:00:30.959 --> 00:00:35.255
Her announcement for that week said: note the key words and definitions,

13
00:00:35.255 --> 00:00:37.462
for example addiction and dependence,

14
00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:41.876
because the learning outcomes for this session will be tested in the exam.

15
00:00:41.876 --> 00:00:46.171
So this module is in the final, and the definitions are the heart of it.

16
00:00:46.621 --> 00:00:48.287
Her own rule for the deck.

17
00:00:48.287 --> 00:00:51.233
On slide three there's a cartoon cat, Pusheen.

18
00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:55.332
If you see Pusheen on a slide, you may be tested on the concept,

19
00:00:55.332 --> 00:00:58.151
but not the statistics or the finer details.

20
00:00:58.151 --> 00:01:03.083
Pusheen sits on the withdrawal symptoms, the substance use disorder criteria,

21
00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:08.463
stimulant or depressant, the slang, the drug combination chart, and every statistic.

22
00:01:08.463 --> 00:01:13.075
So in this episode you'll hear those as ideas, not as lists to memorise.

23
00:01:13.075 --> 00:01:18.455
Everything without Pusheen is fair game in full: the seven terms, licit and illicit,

24
00:01:18.455 --> 00:01:23.131
the risk factors, interactions, where to refer, poisoning, and antidotes.

25
00:01:23.581 --> 00:01:25.823
One correction to carry in with you.

26
00:01:25.823 --> 00:01:30.494
On her first formative mini exam, question four asks what dependence means.

27
00:01:30.494 --> 00:01:32.176
Her answer document says C.

28
00:01:32.176 --> 00:01:36.660
In class on the twentieth she agreed with a student that C is addiction,

29
00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.528
and said the best answer is B:

30
00:01:38.528 --> 00:01:42.327
withdrawal symptoms if a prescribed drug is stopped abruptly.

31
00:01:42.327 --> 00:01:45.192
You'll hear exactly how to tell the two apart.

32
00:01:45.642 --> 00:01:49.188
How she wants a short answer: a definition, plus an example.

33
00:01:49.188 --> 00:01:50.784
Every track gives you both.

34
00:01:50.784 --> 00:01:53.857
The questions you'll hear are this tool's questions,

35
00:01:53.857 --> 00:01:56.103
written in her format from her slides.

36
00:01:56.103 --> 00:02:00.831
Where an answer comes from her own formative or her own words, you'll hear that.

37
00:02:01.281 --> 00:02:02.664
How every track works.

38
00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:04.611
The examiner asks the question.

39
00:02:04.611 --> 00:02:06.999
Then the hook: one line to hang it on.

40
00:02:06.999 --> 00:02:09.826
Then the answer, in the order you'd write it.

41
00:02:09.826 --> 00:02:10.768
Then the traps.

42
00:02:10.768 --> 00:02:14.161
Then the whole answer once more, and you say it first.

43
00:02:14.161 --> 00:02:18.433
The last track, Rapid-fire, is every one-breath answer back to back.

44
00:02:18.883 --> 00:02:22.457
The order: the seven terms first, because she said so.

45
00:02:22.457 --> 00:02:26.694
Then stimulants and depressants, who uses and why, interactions,

46
00:02:26.694 --> 00:02:30.930
the nurse's role and harm reduction, then toxicology: poisoning,

47
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.114
the Poisons Centre and antidotes.

48
00:02:33.114 --> 00:02:36.357
Last, her own formative questions on this module.

49
00:02:36.357 --> 00:02:36.953
Let's go.
